nodecode-myswarm is a rewrite of tomkubik's tomkubik/hermes-myswarm:

  https://github.com/tomkubik/hermes-myswarm
  commit 5a7cf3ced917234a292359ce436c609c3285c3c4
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 MySwarm Contributors (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the whole plugin, in Common Lisp, against the Nodecode
cell contract. The agents.md reader (its four readings: sections, tables,
bullet lines and the plugin's own shared ASCII block), the abbreviated
table, the box-and-arrow topology, the pure 7-bit copy-paste block, the
deterministic PII scrubber and the markdown export, and the import that
keeps the file it replaced and reverts to it, are the original's behaviour
re-expressed over the same text. The original's .svg and .png renderings of
the diagram became the block itself plus an ASCII frame, since a cell writes
text.

What was left out, and why: every model call. The original asked the
operator's model to parse a freeform agents.md, to scrub a second time
contextually, to audit an import, and to art-direct a generated image
(myswarm_visualize_image). A cell that answers the same way whatever model
is talking does the readings with regular expressions only: a freeform file
with no heading, table or bullet becomes one monolithic agent rather than a
model's guess at the agents inside it, the scrubber is the deterministic
stage alone, and the import's security reading is its rule set without the
model pass. The generated themed image is therefore not here. The
original's Hermes-only CLI (`hermes myswarm`) became /myswarm, and its
pre_tool_call approval hook became the verb's own refusals, since Nodecode
asks a person for approval through its own tool gate.
